            <ArticleTitle>Nasal high-flow therapy for type II respiratory failure in COPD: A report of four cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>87-88</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.rmcr.2016.12.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herein we present a report of four cases of severe type II respiratory failure that had contraindications both to conventional non-invasive ventilation and to endotracheal intubation. In all four cases, we successfully used a high-flow nasal oxygen device as a rescue device, with very reassuring outcomes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
